00:32:13.590 --> 00:32:14.130
Pardon me.

00:32:14.190 --> 00:32:15.090
Can I sell you anything else?

00:32:15.630 --> 00:32:17.530
Um, yachting magazine, maybe?

00:32:17.610 --> 00:32:18.150
No, thanks.

00:32:18.870 --> 00:32:19.930
Wonderful thing, sailboats.

00:32:20.340 --> 00:32:21.560
You ever seen anything more beautiful?

00:32:21.860 --> 00:32:22.700
Please, I'm in a hurry.

00:32:23.260 --> 00:32:24.090
Of course you are.

00:32:24.190 --> 00:32:25.010
Everybody's in a hurry.

00:32:25.420 --> 00:32:26.380
That's our big trouble.

00:32:27.200 --> 00:32:30.000
Now, suppose for the sake of argument that you stop to look at this picture.

00:32:30.190 --> 00:32:30.830
How long with it?

00:32:30.850 --> 00:32:32.230
Is there something wrong with the paper?

00:32:32.450 --> 00:32:33.430
No, nothing. I just...

00:32:33.430 --> 00:32:37.730
Well, latest edition, stock market reports, racing results, baseball scores...

00:32:37.730 --> 00:32:39.270
Please, may I just have some change?

00:32:40.620 --> 00:32:43.200
Oh, I don't know, Keith.

00:32:43.920 --> 00:32:45.540
What am I going to do with you?

00:32:45.600 --> 00:32:49.800
Sit around here all day long reading my yachting magazines and drawing pictures of boats.

00:32:50.730 --> 00:32:53.950
And finally, when one crummy little two-bit customer comes along, you can...

00:32:53.950 --> 00:32:56.150
Hey, boss, her change, her change. She's in a hurry.

00:32:56.290 --> 00:32:57.350
Oh, here they are.

00:32:58.490 --> 00:33:00.000
Thank you.

00:33:01.920 --> 00:33:07.320
understand you guy like you working in jobs like this drifting across the

00:33:07.320 --> 00:33:11.640
country a week here two weeks there what kind of a life that I'm having a

00:33:11.640 --> 00:33:17.820
wonderful time that's no excuse intelligent man like you sergeant in the

00:33:17.820 --> 00:33:22.040
army hey pops get off my back I've been out of the country a long time give me a

00:33:22.040 --> 00:33:26.280
couple of months to enjoy it I don't get the psychology of it

00:33:26.280 --> 00:33:30.000
look for 32.50 a week I don't discuss psychology plus 32

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:32.950
now ready for passengers.

00:33:32.950 --> 00:33:36.370
What's the matter? What are you staring at that girl for?

00:33:36.370 --> 00:33:39.410
Boy, what a bus ride that must have been.

00:34:04.380 --> 00:34:07.910
Oh, hello. Does Patricia Monaghan live here?

00:34:07.910 --> 00:34:11.540
She'll use her perfume all the time.

00:34:11.540 --> 00:34:15.790
But she ain't here now.

00:34:15.790 --> 00:34:23.190
Out there?

00:34:23.190 --> 00:34:24.710
No, Patricia.

00:34:24.710 --> 00:34:26.630
Go finish her supper.

00:34:26.630 --> 00:34:28.640
She's gone away. Couldn't stand the heat, I guess.

00:34:28.640 --> 00:34:29.440
Gone away?

00:34:29.440 --> 00:34:30.000
Oh, she'll be back.

00:34:30.640 --> 00:34:31.360
She will when?

00:34:31.920 --> 00:34:33.370
Two or three weeks, she said.

00:34:33.680 --> 00:34:34.560
Two or three weeks?

00:34:35.310 --> 00:34:37.000
Do you know where I can find her?

00:34:37.720 --> 00:34:38.540
Seashore, I guess.

00:34:38.600 --> 00:34:39.200
Maybe the mountains.

00:34:39.280 --> 00:34:39.940
She didn't say.

00:34:40.730 --> 00:34:41.570
Who are you?

00:34:43.190 --> 00:34:46.360
I'm her cousin, Ann Carter.

00:34:48.960 --> 00:34:51.380
Look, I've got to get a job and a place to stay.

00:34:52.030 --> 00:34:53.670
Please, could I stay here?

00:34:54.380 --> 00:34:54.740
Here?

00:34:55.290 --> 00:34:57.400
I'm all filled up except for Patricia's room.

00:34:57.800 --> 00:35:00.000
And if you're her cousin, I guess you know how she can be.

00:35:00.670 --> 00:35:02.450
Better try Mrs. Rollins in the next block.

00:35:02.710 --> 00:35:04.030
The house with the green window boxes.

00:35:04.640 --> 00:35:05.060
Good night.

00:35:46.800 --> 00:35:50.200
- Afternoon, Mr. Murray, is he up there?

00:35:50.200 --> 00:35:54.800
- Yes, sir.

00:35:54.800 --> 00:35:56.060
- So I'd be grateful to you, gentlemen,

00:35:56.060 --> 00:35:57.830
if you'd cooperate in every way you could

00:35:57.830 --> 00:35:58.910
to keep this search in mind.

00:35:58.910 --> 00:36:00.000
- Are these gentlemen reporters

00:36:00.510 --> 00:36:02.030
Why, yes, Mr. Morey, Mr. Rutherford.

00:36:02.030 --> 00:36:03.490
So I was not misinformed.

00:36:03.930 --> 00:36:06.910
Selden, why can't you let her be?

00:36:07.110 --> 00:36:07.710
She's dead.

00:36:07.890 --> 00:36:09.430
I don't care to go over this again.

00:36:09.510 --> 00:36:10.130
I'm sorry if you don't agree with...

00:36:10.130 --> 00:36:12.570
How long can you go on with this publicity?

00:36:13.130 --> 00:36:14.050
It's indecent.

00:36:14.170 --> 00:36:15.470
Look, if she's alive, I've got to find...

00:36:15.470 --> 00:36:16.450
But she's not alive.

00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:18.840
The newspapers are beginning to forget about her.

00:36:19.330 --> 00:36:19.650
Let them.

00:36:19.770 --> 00:36:20.950
I don't want them to forget about her.

00:36:21.530 --> 00:36:22.970
They dragged the whole length of the river,

00:36:23.050 --> 00:36:24.170
but her body was never found.

00:36:24.490 --> 00:36:25.670
I think she is alive.

00:36:25.840 --> 00:36:26.790
I don't know, Mr. Clark.

00:36:27.040 --> 00:36:28.320
I don't see what we can do.

00:36:28.830 --> 00:36:30.000
I'm sorry about the way it's...

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:35.060
sounds but like I've been trying to tell you it's just not news anymore. Want to lift Hank? Fine. What

00:36:35.060 --> 00:36:47.250
if I offered a reward? How big a reward? $5,000. I don't mean to be cynical, but money is always

00:36:47.250 --> 00:36:52.320
news. We could put it on the wires and see what would happen. But if she were alive, why wouldn't

00:36:52.320 --> 00:36:56.940
she have come home? I shouldn't have to tell you, Lucius, but you know what a terrible shock

00:36:56.940 --> 00:37:00.000
her father's death was. How do we know she isn't suffering from anything?

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:04.780
amnesia or some other mental disturbances. Can I quote you, Mr. Clark? No, you cannot. I want

00:37:04.780 --> 00:37:24.050
her back. Yes, you can quote me. This is the latest picture, but one thing, gentlemen, when you write

00:37:24.050 --> 00:37:27.110
your story, I know I can count on you to handle it delicately.

00:37:34.830 --> 00:37:36.090
But I'm sure I tell you.

00:37:36.550 --> 00:37:37.780
I saw this girl.

00:37:38.100 --> 00:37:39.120
Right here in Wally.

00:37:39.750 --> 00:37:40.580
I posited.

00:37:41.300 --> 00:37:42.160
I mean, where?

00:37:42.590 --> 00:37:43.070
Where?

00:37:43.640 --> 00:37:45.620
$5,000 reward.

00:37:45.980 --> 00:37:47.640
I've got to remember where I saw her.

00:37:48.980 --> 00:37:49.480
The pool.

00:37:50.540 --> 00:37:51.180
No?

00:37:51.400 --> 00:37:52.540
Oh, forget it.

00:37:52.890 --> 00:37:53.710
You never saw her.

00:37:54.040 --> 00:37:56.940
You're just overstimulated by the idea of all that money.

00:37:57.000 --> 00:37:57.720
I did see her.

00:37:57.760 --> 00:37:58.480
I know I did.

00:37:59.020 --> 00:38:00.000
Five grand for...

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:05.910
practically in my pocket why can't i remember oh i had to have my head examined now what are you

00:38:05.910 --> 00:38:13.210
doing to the customers what's the matter with you this dame i saw right here and wrong i could get

00:38:13.210 --> 00:38:29.090
the reward five grand only where did i see her where where where where where you too huh

00:38:31.050 --> 00:38:38.260
That's the trouble with everybody. Over-stimulating. Rewards, get rich quick, giveaways on the radio.

00:38:38.500 --> 00:38:42.200
Yeah, I suppose if you collected $5,000, it would ruin your whole day.

00:38:42.480 --> 00:38:47.520
Ah, Pops, if I had $5,000, that little cove on the California coast.

00:38:47.520 --> 00:38:50.660
Yeah, I know. You'd go in the boat building business. You told me all about it, Admiral.

00:38:51.010 --> 00:39:00.000
Hey, wait a minute. Pops were the victims of mass psychology. Now she looks

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:01.080
familiar to me too.

00:39:01.520 --> 00:39:02.080
You see?

00:39:02.490 --> 00:39:03.650
You're a college man.

00:39:04.450 --> 00:39:05.090
Hey, uh, Annie.

00:39:05.350 --> 00:39:06.090
Ham on right.

00:39:07.270 --> 00:39:10.070
Hi, Annie.

00:39:10.590 --> 00:39:11.210
Hot enough for you?

00:39:11.800 --> 00:39:12.120
Uh-huh.

00:39:17.960 --> 00:39:20.330
A chocolate milkshake.

00:39:21.960 --> 00:39:24.850
What's the matter with you?

00:39:26.230 --> 00:39:27.110
Nothing happens.

00:40:04.090 --> 00:40:20.790
the battering thing thomas mr thomas i have to leave right away leave yes right now may i have

00:40:20.790 --> 00:40:25.930
my pay please but annie it's the rush hour i know i'm sorry but it's it's someone in my family

00:40:25.930 --> 00:40:30.000
they're very sick could i have my salary i have three days coming well that's right but

00:40:30.060 --> 00:40:32.200
- Please, Mr. Thomas, please.

00:40:32.200 --> 00:40:34.500
- Well, sure, Annie.

00:40:37.030 --> 00:40:39.850
I'm sorry about the illness in your family.

00:40:39.850 --> 00:40:43.350
Now, if there's anything that I can do...

00:41:18.620 --> 00:41:20.900
Reservations.

00:41:20.900 --> 00:41:23.130
Attention, please.

00:41:23.130 --> 00:41:27.400
Miami to New York Limited will arrive in Raleigh on schedule.

00:41:27.400 --> 00:41:29.860
All seats are reserved.

00:41:30.990 --> 00:41:46.520
I'd like a chocolate bar please. Help yourself, you can find one that's not

00:41:46.520 --> 00:41:55.830
melted. You can just put the money down. We run a very small business here. We trust everybody.

00:42:02.170 --> 00:42:20.700
Bus 32 now ready for passengers to Durham, Goldsville, Winston-Salem, Statesville, Hickory, Black Mountain, Asheville, Newport, Jepson City, Knoxville, and Memphis.

00:42:20.700 --> 00:42:26.950
Please check your baggage, reservations, and make your stopover requests.

00:42:41.000 --> 00:42:41.280
Keith?

00:42:41.740 --> 00:42:42.080
Hi.

00:42:44.190 --> 00:42:48.720
I suppose you're going to tell me you're looking for customers.

00:42:49.000 --> 00:42:49.740
Oh, hello, Pops.

00:42:50.280 --> 00:42:55.040
Look, Keith, I've been meaning to ask you, would you like to do me a big favor?

00:42:55.280 --> 00:42:56.980
Sure, Pops, anything at all, you know that.

00:42:57.180 --> 00:42:57.920
Quit, will you?

00:42:58.630 --> 00:42:59.220
Quit?

00:42:59.530 --> 00:43:00.000
Yeah, it ain't.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:03.260
It ain't right a guy like you should be fired from such a crummy job.

00:43:08.180 --> 00:43:08.580
Okay.

00:43:09.350 --> 00:43:12.430
Wait a minute, it don't have to be right this second.

00:43:12.550 --> 00:43:13.330
You're wrong, Pops.

00:43:13.610 --> 00:43:14.580
I'm afraid it does.

00:43:14.780 --> 00:43:16.660
Well, where are you going?

00:43:16.980 --> 00:43:18.100
I don't know myself just yet.

00:43:18.580 --> 00:43:20.220
I'll write you to let you know where to send the stuff.

00:43:20.620 --> 00:43:26.950
It's for you.

00:43:30.600 --> 00:43:31.200
So long, Admiral.

00:43:33.600 --> 00:43:37.170
Hey, uh, Charlie, that blonde girl who just bought a ticket.

00:43:37.330 --> 00:43:37.790
Where's she going?

00:43:38.190 --> 00:43:39.760
You know I can't tell you that.

00:43:39.990 --> 00:43:41.140
It's against regulation.

00:43:41.500 --> 00:43:42.520
Okay, I'll put it another way.

00:43:42.700 --> 00:43:45.280
I just quit my job, and I'm looking for a vacation spot.

00:43:45.550 --> 00:43:46.160
What do you recommend?

00:43:46.550 --> 00:43:49.140
Cut it out, Charlie.

00:44:01.240 --> 00:44:02.760
My name is Dave Shaw, friends.

00:44:03.200 --> 00:44:05.700
Our first rest stop will be Goldsboro in about two hours.

00:44:06.200 --> 00:44:07.980
Please remain seated while the coach is in motion.

00:45:00.990 --> 00:45:28.070
Anybody want to drink a water or something before we leave?

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:32.420
- No.

00:45:32.420 --> 00:45:36.630
- Tough crowd.

00:45:36.630 --> 00:45:39.880
- Feeling a little shaky?

00:45:39.880 --> 00:45:43.680
- A little.

00:45:43.680 --> 00:45:50.700
- By the way, I owe you an apology,

00:45:50.700 --> 00:45:55.460
just so we don't have the shot.

00:45:55.460 --> 00:45:56.460
When I first got on the bus,

00:45:56.460 --> 00:45:57.840
I thought he was your husband.

00:46:00.030 --> 00:46:04.450
- He isn't, is he?

00:46:30.480 --> 00:46:33.150
You're having a nightmare.

00:46:33.150 --> 00:46:36.160
I woke you up.

00:46:36.160 --> 00:46:37.270
Bad, huh?

00:46:37.270 --> 00:46:38.990
Pretty bad.

00:46:38.990 --> 00:46:43.260
Here, try one of these.

00:46:43.260 --> 00:46:46.740
Supposed to be good for everything else.

00:46:46.740 --> 00:46:49.260
Go on, they'll chase the goblins away.

00:46:49.260 --> 00:46:52.530
They can't stand fire and smoke, you know.

00:47:00.440 --> 00:47:01.280
Want to tell me about it?

00:47:01.890 --> 00:47:03.710
Used to be a whiz with a drain button.

00:47:04.710 --> 00:47:06.170
There's nothing to tell.

00:47:06.690 --> 00:47:07.730
I'm a great listener.

00:47:09.950 --> 00:47:11.990
On the other hand, I'm a great talker, too.

00:47:13.210 --> 00:47:15.160
You've been very nice.

00:47:16.150 --> 00:47:16.550
Thanks.

00:47:17.190 --> 00:47:18.080
Not scared anymore?

00:47:19.080 --> 00:47:19.720
No.

00:47:20.990 --> 00:47:22.800
Why don't you try to get back to sleep, Miss Connor?

00:47:23.440 --> 00:47:25.180
You did say your name was Carter, didn't you?

00:47:26.320 --> 00:47:27.560
Yes, yes, of course.

00:47:27.780 --> 00:47:28.420
And Connor.

00:47:30.250 --> 00:47:32.120
Lean back. Close your eyes.

00:47:33.320 --> 00:47:34.440
No, I don't have...

00:47:34.440 --> 00:47:35.680
I'll watch out for the goblins.

00:47:36.560 --> 00:47:38.600
Seeing as how I have to be in the neighborhood anyway.

00:47:38.980 --> 00:47:40.720
No, I'll be fine, really.

00:48:44.840 --> 00:48:45.820
We're a half hour, folks.

00:48:57.420 --> 00:48:58.800
Mr. Ramsey, I'm very grateful.

00:49:00.250 --> 00:49:01.310
and it saved the farewell address.

00:49:01.370 --> 00:49:02.170
I get off here, too.

00:49:03.770 --> 00:49:04.170
You do?

00:49:04.410 --> 00:49:04.730
Mm-hmm.

00:49:05.450 --> 00:49:07.530
I thought you said you were going to California.

00:49:07.910 --> 00:49:08.450
I am.

00:49:08.760 --> 00:49:09.760
In easy stages.

00:49:10.180 --> 00:49:10.460
Oh.

00:49:10.740 --> 00:49:11.990
I know a couple of people here.

00:49:12.700 --> 00:49:14.370
Kind of a happy coincidence, don't you think?

00:49:15.240 --> 00:49:15.680
Yes.

00:49:15.940 --> 00:49:16.680
Yes, of course.

00:49:17.350 --> 00:49:18.340
Sorry.

00:49:18.800 --> 00:49:19.680
Well, thanks again.

00:49:20.460 --> 00:49:21.920
Maybe we'll run into each other sometime.

00:49:22.540 --> 00:49:25.180
I hate to leave a thing like that entirely at a chance.

00:49:25.660 --> 00:49:26.840
How about dinner tonight?

00:49:27.140 --> 00:49:28.670
No, really, I don't think so.

00:49:28.670 --> 00:49:30.000
Oh, too bad.

00:49:30.760 --> 00:49:35.440
Mr. Ramsey, I don't mean to be unfriendly, but...

00:49:35.440 --> 00:49:35.880
But what?

00:49:36.510 --> 00:49:38.270
Well, you've asked me an awful lot of questions.

00:49:39.040 --> 00:49:41.140
Who I am, where I'm from, where I'm going.

00:49:42.030 --> 00:49:43.120
Why are you so curious about me?

00:49:44.280 --> 00:49:45.020
Particular reason.

00:49:45.430 --> 00:49:47.680
Any reason why I shouldn't be?

00:49:48.240 --> 00:49:50.400
No, I suppose not.

00:49:50.610 --> 00:49:51.280
Of course not.

00:49:52.010 --> 00:49:52.850
Now, about that dinner.

00:49:53.030 --> 00:49:53.910
Well, we'll see.

00:49:54.930 --> 00:49:56.870
You can call me at the hotel this evening if you like.

00:49:57.540 --> 00:49:59.520
Well, anyway, I've got a date for a phone call.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:00.680
Yeah, let me, uh...

00:50:00.680 --> 00:50:03.200
No, really, I can make it to the hotel desk alone, I'm sure.

00:50:03.560 --> 00:50:03.840
Okay.

00:50:04.120 --> 00:50:04.340
Bye.

00:50:05.150 --> 00:50:07.630
Miss Carter, about what time this evening?

00:50:08.800 --> 00:50:10.420
Oh, about 7 o'clock.

00:50:10.720 --> 00:50:11.020
Right.

00:50:11.360 --> 00:50:12.050
Call you at 7.

00:50:13.500 --> 00:50:18.450
The bus for Asheville is now loading.

00:50:19.030 --> 00:50:21.100
You have 10 minutes before departure.

00:50:24.460 --> 00:50:26.260
The bus now loading for Raleigh.

00:50:26.570 --> 00:50:27.660
We'll be leaving shortly.

00:50:28.320 --> 00:50:30.000
Passengers will please start loading.

00:50:46.700 --> 00:50:48.680
Well, the least you can do is meet me.

00:50:49.250 --> 00:50:51.000
What do you expect me to do?

00:50:51.120 --> 00:50:52.120
Walk in this heat?

00:50:54.680 --> 00:50:56.280
Okay, I'll take a cab.

00:50:56.420 --> 00:50:56.740
Goodbye.

00:51:00.570 --> 00:51:03.130
Hello, I'd like to talk to Clarksville, North Carolina, please.

00:51:05.430 --> 00:51:07.590
Person to person to Mr. Selden Clark.

00:51:10.130 --> 00:51:10.590
I'll wait.

00:51:22.210 --> 00:51:25.150
Well, that's that.

00:51:25.610 --> 00:51:27.820
The day after tomorrow, we'll have that machine in full operation.

00:51:28.040 --> 00:51:30.000
You can't do this, Selden. You can't.

00:51:30.960 --> 00:51:31.660
I've done it.

00:51:31.660 --> 00:51:33.160
You have no legal right to.

00:51:33.520 --> 00:51:36.020
You're normally the manager of this mill, not the owner.

00:51:36.020 --> 00:51:37.520
If I'm not, who is?

00:51:37.520 --> 00:51:38.360
Deborah!

00:51:38.360 --> 00:51:40.370
Deborah's dead.

00:51:40.370 --> 00:51:42.300
You finally convinced me.

00:51:42.300 --> 00:51:43.500
Legally, she's not.

00:51:43.500 --> 00:51:45.430
And she won't be for seven years.

00:51:45.430 --> 00:51:47.050
Unless they find her body.

00:51:47.050 --> 00:51:49.550
Until then, we just sit here and let the mill rot, I suppose.

00:51:49.550 --> 00:51:50.750
The law's the law.

00:51:50.750 --> 00:51:52.150
And if someone should challenge you...

00:51:52.150 --> 00:51:53.150
Challenge me?

00:51:53.150 --> 00:51:54.200
Who'd do that?

00:51:54.200 --> 00:51:58.040
As executor of John Chandler's estate, I might.

00:51:58.040 --> 00:51:59.220
Oh, no, you won't.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:03.630
The executor's job is to preserve the estate, not destroy it.

00:52:03.630 --> 00:52:05.130
Don't try to bluff me, Lucius.

00:52:05.130 --> 00:52:06.930
And don't you try to bully me.

00:52:06.930 --> 00:52:09.830
Excuse me, Mr. Clark, but there's a long-distance call for you.

00:52:09.830 --> 00:52:12.130
The man didn't say what it was, but it sounded important.

00:52:12.130 --> 00:52:17.440
Thank you.

00:52:17.440 --> 00:52:25.830
Yes, this is Sultan Clark. Who's this?

00:52:25.830 --> 00:52:28.660
Alive.

00:52:28.660 --> 00:52:29.280
How do you know?

